=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported fault — that VLAN 5 (10.5.0.0/24) and/or VLAN 6 (10.6.0.0/24) hosts on switch4 lost their uplink to the multilayer switch because a VLAN was pruned from the trunk — does not exist in the current lab state. The network is fully healthy.

The trunk between switch4 (eth0) and sshswitch (eth0) carries both VLAN 5 and VLAN 6 as expected. On switch4, the subinterfaces eth0.5 and eth0.6 are both UP, bridged into br_vlan5 and br_vlan6 respectively alongside the correct access ports (eth1–eth3, eth6 for VLAN 5; eth4–eth5 for VLAN 6). On sshswitch, the corresponding eth0.5 and eth0.6 are UP, bridged into br_v5 and br_v6 — the same bridges that hold the layer-3 gateway addresses 10.5.0.254/24 and 10.6.0.254/24. Every VLAN 5 host tested (pc1 at 10.5.0.1, dc_pc5 at 10.5.0.5) reaches its gateway with 0% packet loss; every VLAN 6 host tested (pc3 at 10.6.0.3, pc4 at 10.6.0.4) does the same. Cross-VLAN routing, WAN-side reachability, and remote-campus reachability from VLAN 5 hosts all pass without issue.

The helpdesk ticket is a false premise. No VLAN has been pruned from switch4's trunk, and no corrective action is needed. The maintenance team's concern was not substantiated by the live network state.
=== END ===